Licence: Apache License 2.0. The full text is in the file LICENSE next to this
one (segmenter/vendor/LICENSE). The port's own repository states Apache-2.0 in
its README but ships no LICENSE file, so the standard text is supplied here.

The folder is copied unchanged: not one file was edited. It is vendored because
the repository has no pyproject and is not on PyPI.

The vendored code does `import cv2`. That name is answered by PixelMagic's own
small stand-in, segmenter/src/cv2, not by OpenCV; OpenCV is not a dependency.
The stand-in provides only resize; the vendored video code's blob-labelling call
is not supported (the object finder never reaches it).
